## 7. Scripting System (Reels)

### 7.1 Length strategy
- **Best range: 20–60 seconds** for reach; **60–90 seconds** for tutorials.
- Instagram can create longer Reels (reports say up to 20 minutes), but **recommendations to non-followers are reported to stay capped around 3 minutes**. Keep discovery Reels under 3 minutes.
- Retention beats length: a tight 30s Reel with 80% watch time beats a bloated 90s one.

### 7.2 Master structure

| Time | Part | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| 0–2s | **HOOK** | Stop the scroll |
| 2–7s | **Context / proof** | Show the result or stakes |
| 7–40s | **Value beats (3–5)** | One idea each, new visual every 2–3s |
| 40–50s | **Payoff** | Final result |
| Last 3–7s | **CTA + loop** | One ask, connect back to the hook |

### 7.3 Hook formulas
- **Result-first:** "This free AI did my 2-hour task in 90 seconds."
- **Mistake:** "You're using AI wrong if you prompt like this."
- **Curiosity:** "Nobody's talking about this free AI feature."
- **Number:** "5 AI tools I use every single day."
- **Warning:** "Don't paste this into any AI tool."
- **Comparison:** "Same task, two AIs. One failed."
- **Time:** "Here's how to do X in 60 seconds."

Say it, show it, and write it on screen. No "Hey guys, welcome back."

### 7.4 Script template

```
TITLE (internal):
TARGET VIEWER:
GOAL (share / save / follow / comment / link / DM):

HOOK (0–2s):
  Voice:
  On-screen text:
  Visual:

PROOF (2–7s):
BEAT 1:
BEAT 2:
BEAT 3:
PAYOFF:
CTA:
LOOP LINE:

SOURCES TO VERIFY:
AI LABEL NEEDED? (Y/N):
```

### 7.5 Example Reel script (≈45 sec)

```
HOOK: "This free AI tool turned my messy notes into a full presentation in one minute."
Text: "NOTES → SLIDES IN 60s"
Visual: Fast before/after split screen

PROOF: "Here's the final deck. I didn't design a single slide."

BEAT 1: "Paste your notes and tell it who the audience is."   (screen record, zoom)
BEAT 2: "Add tone and slide count. This part of the prompt matters:" (show prompt)
BEAT 3: "Edit the first two slides yourself so it sounds like you."

PAYOFF: "20-minute job. Two minutes."
CTA: "Comment SLIDES and I'll send you my exact prompt."
```

### 7.6 Example carousel (10 slides)

| Slide | Content |
|---|---|
| 1 | Big promise: "7 free AI tools that save 10 hours/week" |
| 2–8 | One tool per slide: name, what it does, one example, one tip |
| 9 | Recap or bonus tool |
| 10 | CTA: "Save this + send to a friend. Follow for daily AI workflows." |

Carousel rules: first slide = hook, readable text, consistent design, last slide = CTA, aim for saves and sends.

### 7.7 Writing rules
- Write for the ear; short sentences; about 150 words per minute.
- 45-second script ≈ 110–125 words.
- Add a **pattern interrupt** every 3–6 seconds (cut, zoom, text pop, sound).
- Give the viewer something to **try today**.

