## 9. Editing Guide & Quality Standards

### 9.1 Workflow (30–60 min per Reel once practiced)
1. Rough cut: remove silences and mistakes
2. Tighten: cut anything that doesn't move toward the payoff
3. Visual rhythm: change visual every 2–3 seconds
4. Captions: large, high contrast, short lines, check spelling
5. Sound: clear voice first, low music, small effects at transitions
6. Highlights: arrows, circles, zooms on actions
7. Color/brightness: consistent and bright enough
8. Loop: last line leads into the first frame
9. Export 1080×1920 clean (no other app's logo)
10. **Phone test:** sound on and off

### 9.2 Quality checklist
- [ ] Hook works in 2 seconds, even with sound off
- [ ] First frame is not black or a logo
- [ ] Voice is clear; music is low
- [ ] Facts verified; sources saved
- [ ] Text readable on a phone and inside safe zones
- [ ] No TikTok/CapCut/other watermark
- [ ] Music and clips are licensed
- [ ] One clear CTA
- [ ] AI label applied if required
- [ ] Original value added

### 9.3 Targets (practical benchmarks, not official numbers)

| Metric | Healthy target |
|---|---|
| 3-second hold | 65%+ |
| Average watch time | 50%+ of the Reel |
| Sends (shares) per reach | As high as possible; sends are among the strongest signals reported |
| Saves per reach | Higher on tutorials and carousels |
| Follower conversion | 0.5–2% of reach |
| Profile visits → follows | 10%+ |

