## 10. Cover / Thumbnail Guide

Your cover appears on your **profile grid, in search, and in the Reels tab**. Instagram's grid has moved toward a **taller (portrait) crop** instead of a perfect square, and sources differ on the exact ratio, so **preview your grid before posting**.

### 10.1 Specs
- Upload a custom cover at **1080×1920 (9:16)**.
- Keep the **title text and face inside the center safe area** so it survives any grid crop.
- Preview the grid view in the cover editor.

### 10.2 Design rules
1. **One idea, 3–6 words** ("AI Résumé in 60s").
2. **Big bold sans-serif**, high contrast.
3. **Your face or the tool logo** (only where you have the right to show it).
4. **Consistent template:** same fonts, 2–3 brand colors.
5. **Numbers and arrows** attract taps ("5 FREE AI TOOLS").
6. **Max 2 visuals + text**, no clutter.
7. **Series labels** ("AI Workflow #12").
8. **Color-code pillars:** tool demo = blue, news = red, money = green.

### 10.3 Carousel cover
- Slide 1 is your thumbnail. It needs a **clear promise + big title**.
- Keep a consistent layout for slides 2–10 so followers recognize your style.

### 10.4 Grid strategy
Pin your top 3 posts. Keep a consistent look so a new visitor understands your niche in 3 seconds.

