## 11. Captions, Keywords & Hashtags

### 11.1 Caption structure
Instagram now reads captions, on-screen text, and spoken words for **search**. Write like a person searching.

```
Line 1: Keyword-rich hook (what this solves)
Lines 2–4: Extra value, steps, or context
Line 5: One CTA (save / send / comment keyword / link in bio)
Line 6: 3–5 hashtags
```

**Example:**
```
How to turn messy notes into a presentation with free AI tools. Save this for your next deadline and send it to someone who hates making slides. Comment SLIDES and I'll DM you the prompt.
#aitools #productivity #chatgpt #freeaitools #learnai
```

### 11.2 SEO rules
- Put your **main keyword** in: the **spoken audio**, **on-screen text**, **caption**, **alt text**, and **profile name/bio**.
- Use phrases such as "best free AI tools," "AI for students," "how to use ChatGPT for…"
- Reels and public posts can also surface in search engines, so descriptive captions help.

### 11.3 Hashtag rules
- **Use 3–5 relevant hashtags.** Sources say hashtags categorize content but add little reach, and one report says Instagram now limits posts and Reels to five. Don't stuff.
- Mix **1 broad + 2 niche + 1 specific + 1 series/brand**.
- Never use irrelevant viral tags.

