## 13. Trial Reels, Posting Frequency & Scheduling

### 13.1 Trial Reels (use them)
- Trial Reels show your Reel to **non-followers first** without publishing to your followers. Reported as available to public accounts with **1,000+ followers** and now schedulable.
- Use them to **A/B test hooks and covers** before posting publicly.
- If a Trial Reel performs well, publish it to your full audience (or let Instagram auto-share where that option exists).

### 13.2 Frequency

| Stage | Reels/week | Carousels/week | Stories |
|---|---|---|---|
| Launch (days 1–30) | 5–7 | 2–3 | Daily |
| Growth (months 2–4) | 4–5 | 2–3 | Daily |
| Monetized | 3–5 | 2 | Daily |

Sources suggest **3–5 Reels per week** with steady timing helps distribution. Consistency beats bursts.

### 13.3 Best times
- No universal best time. Commonly cited windows: **7–9 AM and 11 AM–1 PM** in your audience's local time, plus evenings.
- Check **Insights → Total followers → Most active times**, test for 2 weeks, then lock in.
- For a US + UK audience, test **UK late morning / US early morning** and **US evening**.

### 13.4 Scheduling
- **Instagram native scheduler** and **Meta Business Suite** let you plan ahead (one report says up to ~75 days in-app; check the current limit).
- Batch-record once or twice a week, schedule the whole week.
- Leave 1–2 open slots weekly for breaking AI news.

