## 14. CTA (Call to Action) Guide

**One CTA per post.** Make it valuable, not begging.

| Goal | CTA examples |
|---|---|
| **Sends** (strong signal) | "Send this to someone who still does this manually." |
| **Saves** | "Save this so you have the prompt later." |
| **Follow** | "Follow for one new AI workflow every day." |
| **Comment keyword → DM** | "Comment PROMPT and I'll DM you my template." |
| **Link click** | "Free checklist at the link in my bio." |
| **Story engagement** | "Vote in my story: which tool should I test next?" |
| **Series** | "Part 2 tomorrow; follow so you don't miss it." |
| **Lead / service** | "DM 'AUTOMATE' to see if I can help your business." |

**Placement:** a short spoken CTA in the last 3–7 seconds, a CTA line in the caption, and a pinned comment. Use Stories to nudge followers toward links and offers.

**DM automation:** If you use a tool to auto-reply to comment keywords, use only reputable tools that follow Meta's platform rules, keep messages helpful, and don't spam.

